From 082ff0ce6b5e6660d0a7392a2139adca4999099b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:05:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM] After an update, Dolby Vision starts from what
 the last build found with the same GPU

The way of drawing a frame of native Dolby Vision (direct or composed, CDVPathChoice) and the fidelity step-down
levels (CDVStepDown) are measured during playback and kept for the next session, under a key of the GPU, its
driver and the build. After any update the key is new, so the first video started from the defaults again. On the
integrated GPU of a Ryzen 9 7950X3D a FEL stream drawn directly, the default, takes 35 to 37 ms of the 41.7 ms of a
refresh at 23.976 Hz and composed 30 ms: the first Dolby Vision video after every update missed one refresh in three
until the two ways had been compared again (README, "Known limits").

Each entry of the memory now names the GPU alone too, with what advancedsettings.xml changes of the work
(DVPathGpu(): the GL_RENDERER without the versions Mesa writes in its last list, LLVM, DRM and the kernel; NVIDIA's
has none). Where the key of this GPU, driver and build has nothing, what the last driver or build found with the
same GPU is where the first video starts (CDVPathMemory::Prior()), for both memories: on that GPU the first FEL
frame is composed. It is measured again as anything recalled is: a way is tried again when the one in use becomes
slower than the other was, or does not fit in the period, and a step-down level goes up as soon as the level above
fits. What a build finds replaces what an older build of the same GPU had, so the prior is always the newest, and a
disk started on two PCs keeps what it knows of each. kodi.log says where each recalled value comes from.

Entries written by Hades up to 1.1 ("<key>=...", without the GPU) are read by their key as before and are no prior
for another: the first update that benefits is the one after this version. Hades up to 1.1 drops the new entries as
not well formed and measures again, as it would after any update.
